VERDICT: APPROVED_WITH_COMMENTS

The project setup and navigation redesign are functionally complete: the tab navigator was replaced by root stack routes, the new home/settings screens are reachable, and the web production export succeeds with the expected routes. TypeScript passes with no errors. The stated visual simplification/removal of content-entry animations is reflected in the moved screens.

Two non-blocking lint warnings remain in `app/index.tsx` for incomplete React Hook dependency arrays; address them before later refactors to avoid stale closures. The lockfile contains incidental npm metadata churn unrelated to declared dependency changes.

Security: none observed; SAST reported no findings.

Next actions: resolve the two hook lint warnings, then manually smoke-test image picking, PDF generation, and settings back navigation on web and native devices before closing the task.

